# Copy to .env. Everything is optional. After a change, run `docker compose up -d` again.

# How a change goes live (default personal):
#   record      each change is recorded and the Host publishes it; nothing checks or approves it.
#   personal    each change is checked; the standing policy approves ordinary changes, the owner decides risky ones.
#   review-all  each change is checked, and the owner decides every change.
# APPGOV_GOVERNANCE=personal

# The risk preset: which change carries which risk, and which risks the standing policy may approve.
# `bun run drive` reads this path on the machine. For the container it is a path inside the container,
# so mount your file there as well. Default: policy/personal.json.
# APPGOV_POLICY_FILE=./policy/personal.json

# Skip starting each draft on PneumaSpace before release (faster, weaker check).
# APPGOV_PREVIEW=off

# Seconds a preview stands: it is a temporary app that ends itself, and a change waiting for the owner keeps it
# until then; approving is refused once it has ended, until `preview <change-id>` publishes it again. PneumaSpace
# refuses more than its ephemeral_max_ttl_seconds (default 3600; raise it with PUT /api/policy first).
# APPGOV_PREVIEW_TTL=3600

# Where the app directories live on this machine (default ./apps). Create the directory yourself first.
# APPGOV_APPS_DIR=./apps

# The four ports, all on 127.0.0.1, the compose project name and the Docker network's name.
# A second stack beside this one needs its own of each (docs/reference.md, "Running beside other services").
# PNEUMA_SPACE_HTTP_PORT=8080
# PNEUMA_SPACE_ADMIN_PORT=8081
# PNEUMA_SPACE_OBJECT_PORT=9000
# APPGOV_HOST_PORT=8090
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=agent-app-governance
# PNEUMA_SPACE_NETWORK=agent-app-governance

# Optional: let undo put an app's PostgreSQL database back after a one-way change (docs/reference.md,
# "Data snapshots for PostgreSQL"). Needs `docker compose --profile postgres up -d` and apps on PostgreSQL
# (PneumaSpace's global policy db_backend=postgres before an app first declares a database). The URL is
# superuser access to every app's database: one trusted machine only.
# APPGOV_DATA_SNAPSHOT=postgres-template
# APPGOV_DATA_SNAPSHOT_URL=postgresql://postgres:pneuma-local@postgres:5432/postgres

# Pictures of apps on the owner page come from the screenshot service (compose.yaml). Empty turns them off:
# the page shows placeholders, and nothing else changes. Hours before a live version is pictured again (default 24).
# APPGOV_SCREENSHOT_CDP=
# APPGOV_SCREENSHOT_REFRESH_HOURS=24

# The name this Host goes by on PneumaSpace as the manager of the apps it releases (default appgov).
# APPGOV_MANAGER=appgov

# The owner of apps created from now on (default user:me); each app keeps its owner in .appgov/app.json.
# If you change it, export the same value in the shell where you run approve, deny and undo --accept-one-way:
# the CLI sends it.
# APPGOV_OWNER=user:me

# Build PneumaSpace from a local checkout instead of the pinned GitHub commit.
# A path to the checkout, not a git URL: compose.yaml appends /cli and /templates to it.
# APPGOV_SPACE_CONTEXT=../../pneuma-space

# Build the Host on a local pneuma-framework checkout instead of the pinned GitHub commit: a path,
# such as the copy `bun run setup` fetched, or another checkout with your own changes.
# APPGOV_FRAMEWORK_CONTEXT=./vendor/pneuma-framework
